      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page (titled \u0022Guarded Write Journal\u0022) describes how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a note that it did not exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n- If the agent run later fails (due to a turn cap, unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content or deleting newly created files.\n- This approach provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, held in process memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback path since it has no write capability.",
